      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Versions with Git",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Each saved document lives in a Git repository. On the History tab, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Save snapshot and upload",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " records a version, and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "View version history",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " lets you browse every snapshot and go back to any of them. Snapshots use your normal Git identity, so they look the same as commits made from the command line.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "level": 1,
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Review: comments, highlights and Overleaf",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "numbered": true,
      "label": null,
      "type": "Section"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Select a passage and press New comment on the Review tab (Ctrl+Alt+M) to leave a note for yourself or a co-author; Accept and Reject sit beside it. Highlight, on the Home tab, marks text without changing it.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
      ],
      "alignment": "justify",
      "type": "Paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Share group on the Review tab works with co-authors on Overleaf: ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Send to Overleaf",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " puts your version into an Overleaf project and ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Get changes from Overleaf",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " brings theirs back. Both need an Overleaf plan with Git access; on a free plan, ",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Download for Overleaf",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ],
          "type": "Text"
        },
        {
          "text": " makes a zip to upload as a new project.",
          "marks": [],
          "type": "Text"
        }
